lse,"description":"Area: Packaging and bundling"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-24T17:47:58Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T13:47:15Z","closed_at":"2025-05-26T13:47:15Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Summary\n\nThe `grammarOverlay` argument is not passed anymore to the Helix package in the flake which prevents users for adding their own grammar overlays.\n\nThe fix seems pretty straight-forward, as far as I can tell. Since the `grammarOverlays` still exists in `grammars.nix`, we just need to update `default.nix` to take as another argument the `grammarOverlays` again, like so:\n\n```nix\n{\n  lib,\n  rustPlatform,\n  callPackage,\n  runCommand,\n  installShellFiles,\n  git,\n  gitRev ? null,\n  grammarOverlays ? []\n}: let\n  # --snip--\n\n  grammars = callPackage ./grammars.nix { inherit grammarOverlays; };\n  # ...\n```\n\n### Reproduction Steps\n\n<!-- Ideally provide a key sequence and/or asciinema.org recording. --> \n\nHere are the reproduction steps:\n\n1. Import the Helix flake in your flake\n2. Use the provided package\n3. Override the package with `.override { grammarOverlays = []; }`\n\nI expected this to happen:\n\nBeing able to pass a grammar overlay to the derivation.\n\nInstead, this happened:\n\nThe package fails to build with a grammar overlay provided with `.override`.\n\n\n### Helix log\n\n\nN/A\n\n### Platform\n\nNixOS\n\n### Terminal Emulator\n\nTTY\n\n### Installation Method\n\nflake\n\n### Helix Version\n\nmaster","closed_by":{"login":"the-mikedavis","id":21230295,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMjMwMjk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21230295?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/the-mikedavis","html_url":"htt